// Activity on the web host: the page opens when asked for, shows its status line and Refresh, and keeps standing while the clock moves.
// The number of asks is not visible to a contract test (`expect no failures` did not catch the 2026-11-28 storm: about 60 asks a second here); it is held by
// exact-facts.test.ts H3 (no resource reads the clock; Activity is asked only with its page on top) and measured in docs/changes/2026-11-28-activity-asked-per-frame.md.
// The web host has no account, so no rows are fetched; the ages are the contract's `agoText` (activity.contract), checked in the change entry.
//  A1 before the Activity page is on top its status line is not drawn; once opened it is, and Refresh is there.
//  A2 the clock moving does not take the page away or fail anything.
//  A3 Refresh leaves the page answered.
test "Activity: opens on press, and stands while the clock moves"
  clock data
  tap "bar-mark"
  clock settle
  expect tree missing "activity-status"
  tap "place-activity"
  clock data
  clock settle
  expect tree has "activity-status"
  expect tree has "activity-refresh"
  clock +5000
  clock settle
  clock +5000
  clock settle
  expect tree has "activity-status"
  expect no failures

test "Activity: Refresh asks again and the page stays answered"
  clock data
  tap "bar-mark"
  clock settle
  tap "place-activity"
  clock data
  clock settle
  tap "activity-refresh"
  clock data
  clock settle
  expect tree has "activity-status"
  clock +5000
  clock settle
  expect no failures
